<Base title="Charlie Kerfoot">
  <h1 class="title">Charlie Kerfoot</h1>

  <p>
    I'm currently building <a href="https://lyriel.ai">Lyriel</a>, the
    substrate for agent-mediated communication. I'm also a student at the
    University of Chicago studying Computer Science and Philosophy.
  </p>

  <p>
    Previously, I was obsessed with
    <a href="https://github.com/CharlieKerfoot/swarm">agentic orchestration</a>
    and CUA tools, made a
    <a href="https://commoncents.fun">browser game</a>, built an 8-bit
    computer on breadboards, and did
    <a href="https://tokenprobe.cs.columbia.edu/">AI research</a> at
    Columbia as a junior in high school.
  </p>

  <p>
    I spend the vast majority of my time either
    <a href="https://github.com/charliekerfoot">coding</a> or
    <a href="/blogs/fiction/">reading</a> (about 70/30 split). I write occasionally 
    covering whatever my mind is enamored with at the moment
    (<a href="/blogs/">Best Foot Forward</a>).
  </p>

  <p>
    You can reach me at
    <a href="mailto:charliekerfoot@gmail.com">charliekerfoot@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
